=== Gap found ===

Grepped for an idempotency guard around _endGuidedTopicTeaching (e.g.
_guidedTopicTeachingEndInFlight or similar) — none exists. Two independent
completion signals (model tool call via the directive; the 5-minute
backstop timer) both call the same _endGuidedTopicTeaching() function with
nothing serializing them — a genuine, if narrow, race: the model calling
the tool right as the backstop's periodic 15s check also trips, or a
duplicate directive over a flaky transport. Each entry independently
drains audio then calls _hide() + fires onGuidedTopicTeachingEnd ->
completePractice(topicId) a second time for the same topic.

Also checked whether end_teaching_session's server-side
`(session as any).teacherModeEnded = true;` pattern (Teacher Mode, a
sibling feature) was worth mirroring for guided-topic teaching, to reject
new AI turns server-side after completion:
$ grep -rn "teacherModeEnded" services/gateway/src
-> only ONE occurrence (the assignment itself) — nothing in the codebase
   ever reads this flag. It is dead state in the sibling feature, not a
   proven protective mechanism. Not copied — see acceptance.md's
   "Deliberately NOT attempted" section for the reasoning.

=== Implementation ===

Edited services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js:
  1. Declared _guidedTopicTeachingEnded: false in the widget's state
     object, alongside the sibling guided-topic lifecycle flags.
  2. _endGuidedTopicTeaching(topicId, reason): added the guard check +
     set as the first synchronous statement, before `var attempts = 0;`
     and before any setTimeout is scheduled.
  3. focusGuidedTopic(topicId): reset _s._guidedTopicTeachingEnded = false
     alongside the other fresh-tap resets (audio-delivered flag,
     zero-audio-fail counter).

